6772403717,0.0,-0.9644181728363037,-7.152555099310121e-07,0.0,0.0,-5.960462772236497e-07,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.005735369399189949,0.0,-1.6689286894688848e-06,-3.099436753473128e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"To solve the given system of equations involving complex numbers, we start with the first equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| = 1.\n\\]\n\nThis implies that the magnitudes of the numerator and the denominator are equal, so we can write:\n\n\\[\n|z - 4| = |z - 8|.\n\\]\n\nThis means that the point \\(z\\) is equidistant from the points 4 and 8 on the complex plane. The locus of points equidistant from two fixed points is the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining these points. The midpoint of 4 and 8 is 6, and the perpendicular bisector is the vertical line \\( \\text{Re}(z) = 6 \\). Therefore, we can write:\n\n\\[\nz = 6 + bi,\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(b\\) is a real number. Now, we substitute \\(z = 6 + bi\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(z = 6 + bi\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{6 + bi - 12}{6 + bi - 8i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3} \\implies \\left| \\frac{-6 + bi}{6 + (b-8)i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of a complex number \\(\\frac{a+ci}{d+ei}\\) is \\(\\frac{|a+ci|}{|d+ei|}\\), so we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{|-6 + bi|}{|6 + (b-8)i|} = \\frac{5}{3} \\implies \\frac{\\sqrt{36 + b^2}}{\\sqrt{36 + (b-8)^2}} = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\n\n","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,9885,678,6351,5109,400,89,3,1741,429,198,59,7265,90,6612,9,532,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,19,15170,89,481,220,23,92,1124,1291,91,14581,220,16,11,90155,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,16,17,15170,89,481,220,23,72,92,1124,1291,91,14581,1124,37018,90,20,15170,18,27275,59